{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/904465-ephemeral-vassalage-\u2013-merits","id":904465,"title":"Ephemeral Vassalage \u2013 Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T14:43:27-07:00","id":904465,"title":"Ephemeral Vassalage \u2013 Merits","content":"Another set of Merits I've been futzing around with to represent a personal tie to a greater entity, both the benefits and perils of the relationship. Any thoughts/input would be appreciated. Should work for any splat, although there are probably some that work better than others.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Vassal Merits</b><br /> <br /> By tying one\u2019s Fate and will to an ephemeral being of great power, individuals are able to harness their power and authority. This comes at a price however, as you are bound to your patron\u2019s will as well, and its weaknesses bleed into you as well. <br /> Anyone capable of meetings the prerequisites can be so bound. There have been werewolf Vassals of the Underworld and Sin-Eater Vassals of the Shadow. Frequently, mortal cultists or mediums use this as a shortcut to power, thinking (mistakenly) that they can someone avoid the more unpleasant aspects. The most limited group of Supernal Vassals, since only Awakened mages and grail-bearers can normally summon a Supernal entity. <br /> Vassals frequently have other related Merits like Familiar, Astral Adept (for Astral Vassals), Dream (for Astral Vassals), Mystery Cult Influence or Mystery Cult Initiation, Mentor, etc. Mages will often use this Vassalage as a Shadow Name as well.<br /> The Exarchs are possessive entities, and will not allow their servants to have any other masters; Vassalage is not compatible with the Merit Prelacy. Similarly, Forsaken who have joined a Lodge cannot have a Vassalage.<br /> <br /> <b>Vassal, Supernal (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> Prerequisites: At least 2 dots in the primary Arcanum of the Patron, have summoned a Supernal entity of at least Rank 3, cannot have the Prelacy Merit<br /> Effect:<br /> \u2022 Vassal - You are officially aligned with a specific Supernal Entity, and have willingly entered its service. Add 2 dice to any summoning attempts for your Patron, and subtract 2 dice from attempts to summon other entities. You gain the persistent Mystery Commands Condition, attuned to your patron. Your bond can be detected using Prime Mage Sight. You also gain a Rank 1 Ban associated with your Patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Page - Add three dice to any summoning attempts for your Patron. You can now expand the safe area for your patron to a space as big as your Demesne/Sanctum (whichever is larger). You can also extend how long your patron can stay by burning 1 Mana instead of having it lose Corpus. (This cannot be done for other forms of Corpus damage).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Squire - Once per session you can call upon your patron to gain Mana equal to the patron\u2019s Rank. Mana in excess of your normal carrying capacity can be spent the turn it is called, but will disappear the next turn if unused. Using this automatically activates the Obsession Condition for one your patron\u2019s commands until it is completed. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Knight - Your patron teaches you 1 Rote per Rank divide by 2 (round up). The rote must be from its primary Arcanum, and can have a maximum Arcanum rating of the patron\u2019s rank. If this exceeds your normally ability to case, you can still use the rote by spending 1 Mana and risking Paradox as if you\u2019d exceeded free Reach by 1. You gain a Rank 2 Ban associated with your patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Champion - Gain a custom Attainment based on your patron\u2019s purview. Add one automatic success to every roll to summon your patron. Gain the bane of your patron. Revealing the bane to another creature results in the immediate cessation of the Vassalage and the loss of the your soul. No magical force can compel you to reveal the bane.<br /> <br /> <b>Vassal, Shadow (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> Prerequisites: Bargain with a spirit of at least Rank 4, the ability to perceive and speak with spirits, cannot have the Prelacy Merit<br /> Effect:<br /> \u2022 Vassal - You have been marked by your patron; any spirits of your patron\u2019s court experience the Open Condition within 10 yards of you. You gain the persistent Mystery Commands Condition, attuned to your patron. Reduce the numbers of doors by 2 when interacting with spirits of your court. Your bond can be detected using Spirit Mage Sight. You also gain a Rank 1 Ban associated with your Patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Page - While in your presence, court spirits are safe from essence bleed. You gain an effective spirit Rank of 1 for all purposes.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Squire - Once per session you can call upon your patron to gain Mana equal to the patron\u2019s Rank. Mana in excess of your normal carrying capacity can be spent the turn it is called, but will disappear the next turn if unused. Using this automatically activates the Obsession Condition for one your patron\u2019s commands until it is completed. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Knight - You gain an effect spirit Rank of 2 for all purposes. Your patron teaches you 1 Numina per 2 Ranks (round up). Activating a Numina costs one point of Mana, but does not cause Paradox or Quiescence.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Champion - Gain a custom Attainment based on your patron\u2019s purview. Gain the bane of your patron. Revealing the bane to another creature results in the immediate cessation of the Vassalage and the loss of the your soul. No magical force can compel you to reveal the bane.<br /> <br /> <b>Vassal, Underworld (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> Prerequisites: Bargain with a ghost/Chthonic entity of at least Rank 4, the ability to perceive and speak with ghosts, cannot have the Prelacy Merit<br /> Effect:<br /> \u2022 Vassal - You have been marked by your patron; any ghosts aligned with your patron experience the Open Condition within 10 yards of you. You gain the persistent Mystery Commands Condition, attuned to your patron. Reduce the numbers of doors by 2 when interacting with any ghosts. Your bond can be detected by Death Mage Sight. You also gain a Rank 1 Ban associated with your Patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Page - While in your presence, ghosts are safe from essence bleed. Ghosts taking advantage of this must provide 1 service to you for each day they take advantage of it.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Squire - Once per session you can call upon your patron to gain Mana equal to the patron\u2019s Rank. Mana in excess of your normal carrying capacity can be spent the turn it is called, but will disappear the next turn if unused. Using this automatically activates the Obsession Condition for one your patron\u2019s commands until it is completed. Ghosts of rank 1 will never attack your character unless attacked first, and at the cost of 1 Willpower point can be issued a simple command. This will invoke a Clash of Wills. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Knight - Your patron teaches you 1 Numina per 2 Ranks (round up). Activating a Numina costs one point of Mana, but does not cause Paradox or Quiescence. You gain a Rank 2 Ban associated with your patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Champion - Gain a custom Attainment based on your patron\u2019s purview. Ghosts of rank 2 will never attack you unless they\u2019re attacked first, and at the cost of 1 Willpower point can be issued a simple command. Gain the bane of your patron. Revealing the bane to another creature results in the immediate cessation of the Vassalage and the loss of the your soul. No magical force can compel you to reveal the bane.<br /> <b>Vassal, Astral(\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> Prerequisites: Bargain with a goetic entity of at least Rank 4, the ability to access the Temenos, cannot have the Prelacy Merit<br /> Effect:<br /> \u2022 Vassal - Your bond can be detected by Mind Mage Sight. You also gain a Rank 1 Ban associated with your Patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Page - Increase your Willpower trait by one. Goetica of rank 1 will never attack your character unless attacked first, and at the cost of 1 Willpower point can be issued a simple command. This will invoke a Clash of Wills. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Squire - Once per chapter you can call upon your patron to gain Willpower equal to the patron\u2019s Rank. Willpower in excess of your normal carrying capacity can be spent the turn it is called (following normal Willpower spending limits), but will disappear the next turn if unused. Using this automatically activates the Obsession Condition for one your patron\u2019s commands until it is completed. <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Knight - Gain an Influence at a level equal to half your patron\u2019s rank (round up) related to your patron\u2019s influences. The activation roll to use the Influence is Presence + Wits. You gain a Rank 2 Ban associated with your patron.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Champion - Gain a custom Attainment based on your patron\u2019s purview. Increase your Willpower trait by 2. Gain the bane of your patron. Revealing the bane to another creature results in the immediate cessation of the Vassalage and the loss of the your soul. No magical force can compel you to reveal the bane.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:44:35-07:00","id":904468,"title":"","content":"Here are a couple of example Patrons I also put together<br /> <b>Styrius, Lord of the Bloodless Dead</b><br /> Appearing as a pristine corpse, drained of all blood and fluid, holding an obsidian cup always dripping some foul ichor, obsessed with removing any trace of blood<br /> Realm: Underworld / Ghost<br /> Rank: 4<br /> Ban (1): If a foe is slain, the body must be drained of blood before you can leave<br /> Ban (2) Must exsanguinate one person a month<br /> Bane: A potion crafted from the heart\u2019s blood of a person<br /> Attainment: Lethal wounds can be downgraded to Bashing by spending 1 Willpower per injury.<br /> Obsessions (examples)<ul><li>Ensure that every body in a particular morgue is properly and fully embalmed</li> <li>Completely drain the blood from a vampire</li> <li>Get an individual to bleed themself to death</li> <li>Remove any/all bloodstains from a series of crime scenes</li> </ul><b>Archon, Senecheal of the Abiding Light</b><br /> An angelic figure with seven wings of broken glass and eyes that pierce any illusion or lie. Will not tolerate any lie, no matter how small or well intentioned, and will punish offenders with a rain of crystal shards<br /> Realm: Supernal / Aether (Prime &amp; Mind)<br /> Rank: 5<br /> Ban (1): Never tell a lie, either actively or by omission<br /> Ban (2): Must inflict at least one level of bashing damage on anyone lying to him<br /> Bane: A pen used by a man/woman who has never lied<br /> Attainment: Spend 1 Willpower to make any individual tell the complete and unmitigated truth for an entire scene.<br /> Rotes: Pierce Deception (Prime 1, automatic +1 reach to sense the actual truth), Words of Truth (Prime 2), Create Truth (Prime 5)<br /> Obsessions(examples)<ul><li>Ensure that someone who has lied while on trial is permanently disfigured in a way that reflect the lie</li> <li>Collect the tongues of seven convicted perjurers</li> <li>Reveal the Truth of the Supernal to seven Sleepers</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:05:16-07:00","id":904484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vassal, Shadow</b><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Squire - Once per session you can call upon your patron to gain <i><b><u>Mana </u></b></i>equal to the patron\u2019s Rank. <i><b><u>Mana </u></b></i>in excess of your normal carrying capacity can be spent the turn it is called, but will disappear the next turn if unused. Using this automatically activates the Obsession Condition for one your patron\u2019s commands until it is completed. </div> </div> </div>I think this there is a mistake here. Spirits don\u00b4t have mana, but essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:10:06-07:00","id":904486,"title":"","content":"What benefits do the fifth dot grant to non-Mages? And what do they spend in place of Mana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:20:02-07:00","id":904493,"title":"","content":"Raistlin - You're right - I originally wrote it from a Mage point of view and then expanded it. I would say that it provides whatever fuel stat your splat uses (Essence, Vitae, Plasm, Mana, etc.) Not sure how it would impact mortals - perhaps Willpower?<br /> <br /> Zealous - Attainment is probably a leftover term as well. Perhaps just &quot;supernatural ability&quot; as the name? The example attainments I created are fueled by Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2947,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","user":"ForgeEternal","date":". 05-31-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:27:46-07:00","id":904501,"title":"","content":"Mortal may be unable to use essence themselves, but they stil can offer it to spirits and werewolves to grease the wheels of any negotiation. In any case, spending 4 or more points of Essence in the same turn may be difficult even for a major splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 06-01-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:59:21-07:00","id":904931,"title":"","content":"Good point for the mortal 'bargaining chip' use of the essence. As for the major splats, they can absorb the essence/mana/etc normally, up to their maximum. It's only excess that is lost. Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2947-forgeeternal","name":"ForgeEternal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}